@startuml
title Visitor / Double Dispatch

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Add operations to object structures without changing elements.

**Motivation**:
Need to add operations frequently; elements are stable.

**Applicability**:
Stable element hierarchy, frequently changing operations.

**Participants**:
Element.accept(visitor) calls back visitor.visit(this).

**Consequences**:
Pros: Add operations without modifying elements; separation of concerns.
Cons: Hard to add new element types (touch many visitors); double-dispatch boilerplate.

**Implementation Notes**:
Use over composite structures; consider Acyclic Visitor to mitigate dependencies.

**Known Uses**:
Compilers/linters; XML/JSON tree processing.

**Related Patterns**:
Composite, Iterator, Interpreter.

endlegend

interface Visitor {
  +visitElementA(e: ConcreteElementA)
  +visitElementB(e: ConcreteElementB)
}

class ConcreteVisitor1
class ConcreteVisitor2

Visitor <|.. ConcreteVisitor1
Visitor <|.. ConcreteVisitor2

interface Element {
  +accept(v: Visitor)
}

class ConcreteElementA
class ConcreteElementB

Element <|.. ConcreteElementA
Element <|.. ConcreteElementB

ConcreteElementA ..> Visitor : accept/visit
ConcreteElementB ..> Visitor : accept/visit
@enduml